    "description": "InPACdb, the Indian Plant Anticancer Compounds Database, is a free online resource cataloging phytochemicals. The goal is to highlight the anticancer potential of plant-based compounds from traditional Indian medicine. This database uniquely provides details about cancer types, molecular targets, 3D structures, and chemical properties for each entry, facilitating in-depth analysis. The complete dataset, with extensive information for each compound, can be freely downloaded from the InPACdb website.\n\nLicense: Data available on Github no license",
